PATCH_ID: 001
TYPE: architecture_setup

INTENT:
Establish deterministic GitHub intake + Claude Code execution pipeline.

CONTEXT:
Repo is used as a structured execution queue. GPT produces patch packets, GitHub stores intent, Claude Code processes and outputs diffs/files.

SCOPE:
- github/intake structure
- github/outbox structure
- patch format standard
- processing rules

CHANGES:

- Create folder structure:
  - github/intake/gpt/
  - github/intake/claude/
  - github/outbox/claude/
  - github/outbox/gpt/
  - github/archive/

- Define standard patch packet format:
  - PATCH_ID (unique)
  - TYPE (feature/refactor/fix/cleanup)
  - INTENT (single sentence)
  - CONTEXT (minimal)
  - SCOPE (max 5 files recommended)
  - CHANGES (atomic list)
  - CONSTRAINTS (mandatory)
  - OUTPUT EXPECTED

- Define intake processing rules:
  - GPT writes intent-only packets into /intake/gpt
  - Claude validates and may split tasks
  - Valid tasks move to /intake/claude
  - Execution outputs go to /outbox/claude

- Define Claude execution contract:
  - Input: scoped files + constraints
  - Output: unified diff OR full file replacement
  - Must not expand architecture
  - Must remain within requested scope

- Define splitting rule:
  - If >1 intent → split patch
  - If >5 files → split patch
  - If ambiguous → reject or request clarification

- Define safety constraint:
  - no new systems or architecture layers
  - no global refactors unless explicitly requested
  - no hidden dependencies

CONSTRAINTS:
- no runtime changes required
- no emulator integration yet
- no execution code required
- documentation-level setup only

OUTPUT EXPECTATION:
- GitHub folder structure ready for intake pipeline
- Claude Code can consume /intake/gpt as queue
- deterministic patch → execution → outbox flow established
